 28864 |     auto result_ = at::sym_stride(self_base, dim_base);
       |                    ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~
       |                    compositeimplicitautograd::sym_stride
/tmp/eugo/pytorch/build/aten/src/ATen/ops/sym_stride_compositeimplicitautograd_dispatch.h:20:23: note: 'compositeimplicitautograd::sym_stride' declared here
   20 | TORCH_API c10::SymInt sym_stride(const at::Tensor & self, int64_t dim);
      |                       ^
4 warnings and 4 errors generated.
This fails because my sym_size.h, etc are using the dynamic dispatcher:
#pragma once

// @generated by torchgen/gen.py from Function.h

#include <ATen/Context.h>
#include <ATen/DeviceGuard.h>
#include <ATen/TensorUtils.h>
#include <ATen/TracerMode.h>
#include <ATen/core/Generator.h>
#include <ATen/core/Reduction.h>
#include <ATen/core/Tensor.h>
#include <c10/core/Scalar.h>
#include <c10/core/Storage.h>
#include <c10/core/TensorOptions.h>
#include <c10/util/Deprecated.h>
#include <optional>
#include <string_view>

#include <ATen/ops/sym_size_compositeimplicitautograd_dispatch.h>

#include <ATen/ops/sym_size_ops.h>

namespace at {

// aten::sym_size.int(Tensor self, int dim) -> SymInt
inline c10::SymInt __dispatch_sym_size(const at::Tensor & self, int64_t dim) {
return at::_ops::sym_size_int::call(self, dim);
}

}
and UnboxingFunctions_0.cpp expects at::sym_size to exist in the public API so sym_size and the other symbolic functions are not found. I understand these symbolic functions are treated differently (i.e. MANUAL_BACKEND dict in gen_trace_type.py).
I've traced the issue to gen.py and native_functions.yaml w/ the manual_cpp_binding: True. Is it possible the manually implemented symbolic functions were missed in Functions.h or FunctionsManual.cpp?

(4) manual_cpp_bindings and faithful names are not included in the API.
This applies to stuff like __dispatch__is_complex(), and add_outf().
These aren't "real aten ops", they're just additional functions provided by the C++ API.
They're implemented as wrappers in Functions.h that call into the actual operators
defined here, i.e. at::_ops::is_complex::call() and at::_ops::add_out::call().
This means that ATEN_OP(is_complex) will not fastpath, and will go through the dispatcher.`

For example the following code exists in Functions.h:
// These are manually defined wrappers:
inline int64_t numel(const Tensor& tensor) {
  return tensor.numel();  // Calls tensor method
}

inline int64_t size(const Tensor& tensor, int64_t dim) {
  return tensor.size(dim);  // Calls tensor method
}

inline int64_t stride(const Tensor& tensor, int64_t dim) {
  return tensor.stride(dim);  // Calls tensor method
}
Appreciate the help.
